  "summary": "Advocates in Kyle, Texas are urging the City Council to reject an expansion of its Flock Safety license plate reader program and reduce the 25 ALPRs and 3 live-view cameras currently deployed, citing privacy and false-positive concerns. The push follows Austin's recent termination of its Flock contract and San Marcos's rejection of a Flock proposal. Kyle police defend the program, citing crime-solving uses and audit policies.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Last month, the city of Austin ended its contract with Flock and San Marcos rejected a proposal from the company to expand its program.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "There are such large discrepancies between the population size and the amount of cameras per person in the city of Kyle",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "We assure our community that comprehensive policies, restricted access, and regular audits are in place to govern the appropriate use of these systems",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    }
